00:39:02,340 --> 00:39:05,844
I'll make sure the Republicans don't
come to my candidate's defense.

600
00:39:11,557 --> 00:39:13,476
I was in a really bad place.

601
00:39:16,562 --> 00:39:18,314
I couldn't do anything.

602
00:39:20,441 --> 00:39:22,235
I couldn't leave my apartment.

603
00:39:23,403 --> 00:39:24,529
Why?

604
00:39:25,530 --> 00:39:29,910
It's mysterious, isn't it,
when these things happen?

605
00:39:29,993 --> 00:39:31,953
Or maybe it never happened to you.

606
00:39:32,037 --> 00:39:35,206
But I woke up one day
and it felt like...

607
00:39:36,917 --> 00:39:40,003
everything I contemplated
doing, everything,

608
00:39:40,086 --> 00:39:42,797
from going to the coffee shop...

609
00:39:42,881 --> 00:39:47,385
to... reading a book, writing
a chapter, it was just...

610
00:39:49,137 --> 00:39:50,555
laughable.

611
00:39:53,183 --> 00:39:54,225
As in?

612
00:39:55,560 --> 00:39:58,479
As in... pointless.

613
00:40:01,024 --> 00:40:03,234
And Karen, bless her...

614
00:40:04,319 --> 00:40:07,488
she helped me find a point.
Or, not find one.

615
00:40:08,573 --> 00:40:11,659
Realize the possibility of one.

616
00:40:15,413 --> 00:40:16,664
Were you together?

617
00:40:16,747 --> 00:40:19,375
Yeah. We were married.

618
00:40:20,376 --> 00:40:23,504
For about three years.
A million years ago.

619
00:40:25,506 --> 00:40:27,133
She's a good person.

620
00:40:27,217 --> 00:40:31,262
She's just... having a hard time.
So I'm trying to help her.

621
00:40:37,060 --> 00:40:39,312
- Find a point?
- Mmm-hmm.

622
00:40:43,274 --> 00:40:45,193
You ever been that dark?

623
00:40:49,280 --> 00:40:51,199
I wanna be with you.

624
00:40:56,412 --> 00:40:57,830
I love you.

625
00:41:00,333 --> 00:41:02,585
I think I might love you, too.

626
00:41:10,218 --> 00:41:12,928
That's the script for
the 30-second spot.

627
